 "title": "GTA 6 just broke Australia's internet record on launch night",
 "audio": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3Lh3gaSoJDsjYAzqFyj65XamsxE/hf_20261119_053250_5d75f93f-978c-4d8a-8286-d4e5cf544f6d.wav",
 "script": "GTA 6 just broke Australia's internet record. On launch night, the national network peaked at 36.54 terabits per second. NBN Co says that's enough to download all 212 gigabytes of GTA 6 about 21 times every second. That's about 20 percent above a normal night. The old record was set only last week. In that week alone, Aussies downloaded roughly 70 petabytes extra, about 330,000 copies. Did you preload, or leave it to launch night? Comment which one.",
